{"text":"At eight, I built a home for birds. Fair and tight, made of neat pop sticks from school, the door was a yawn in a red-brown throat, the house a flesh of sorts. Soon, I saw that space is a war for home, a war for that which we were too proud to name. Air crawls inside thick as a toad. Last, inward waltz, ants black and sharp as full-stop jazz notes, they were like a beat or like an ache, a gang of quick welts. Like a womb, the dark in the house vibes hot and deep. In the way, way back, so far that my eyes see just fuzz, there could be a lake in heat where waves whirl like blue snakes. Their glue melts and croaks, so full it is with a damp that has sat there all day with her thighs shut. Can you see in a house for birds? The truth? No. The truth too? Yes, but just in sleep, if my mouth dries and pain shoots up my left leg like vines that wake round a trunk.","words":[{"text":"At","start":0.0,"end":0.7},{"text":"eight","start":0.7,"end":1.02,"punct":","},{"text":"I","start":1.54,"end":1.74},{"text":"built","start":1.74,"end":1.98},{"text":"a","start":1.98,"end":2.2},{"text":"home","start":2.2,"end":2.56},{"text":"for","start":2.56,"end":3.04},{"text":"birds","start":3.04,"end":3.54,"punct":"."},{"text":"Fair","start":4.24,"end":4.3},{"text":"and","start":4.3,"end":4.6},{"text":"tight","start":4.6,"end":5.02,"punct":","},{"text":"made","start":5.42,"end":5.76},{"text":"of","start":5.76,"end":5.98},{"text":"neat","start":5.98,"end":6.24},{"text":"pop","start":6.24,"end":6.54},{"text":"sticks","start":6.54,"end":6.94},{"text":"from","start":6.94,"end":7.28},{"text":"school","start":7.28,"end":7.9,"punct":","},{"text":"the","start":8.12,"end":8.16},{"text":"door","start":8.16,"end":8.52},{"text":"was","start":8.52,"end":9.0},{"text":"a","start":9.0,"end":9.2},{"text":"yawn","start":9.2,"end":9.6},{"text":"in","start":9.6,"end":10.16},{"text":"a","start":10.16,"end":10.28},{"text":"red-brown","start":10.28,"end":10.98},{"text":"throat","start":10.98,"end":11.42,"pu